-- Fishing spots for pool bots: the FISH_LOCATION rows of the travel fish table.
--
-- Source: T-imothy/tortoise-wow, branch mantech-turtle at 0fb4d7c (read 2026-10-13),
--   modules/mod-playerbots/sql/world/classic/ai_playerbot_named_location.sql
--   blob 7497bbaf676de591ba53b401d8d1454e69e7a1e7, last changed by 8415f1b.
--   Donor lineage: Shyalya mod-playerbots, classic cmangos HeidiSQL dump
--   (54,055 rows = 54,038 FISH_LOCATION rows + 17 AV named points).
-- Data-only port: the DROP and CREATE header is omitted. The schema
--   stays owned by 20260824090000_world.sql. The dump has no licence header.
--   The owner approved shipping it on 2026-10-13 (docs/LICENSE_AUDIT.md).
--
-- Why it ships: TravelMgr::LoadFishLocations reads the FISH_LOCATION rows. A
--   fresh server has none and fish-location generation is disabled, so
--   GetFishSpot never returns a spot and pool bots fall back to open water.
--
-- Shipped: 52,766 rows, all on map 0 (Eastern Kingdoms) and map 1 (Kalimdor).
-- Left out of the dump:
--   1,264 rows on instance maps 36, 43, 48, 289, 309, 349 (dungeon and raid pools).
--     Pool bots are overworld only (WorldPosition::isOverworld), so these are
--     not spots a bot should travel into.
--   8 rows with z = -200000, the no-terrain sentinel:
--     FISH_LOCATION_0_171_45038
--     FISH_LOCATION_0_171_45034
--     FISH_LOCATION_0_171_45030
--     FISH_LOCATION_0_591_37788
--     FISH_LOCATION_0_591_37787
--     FISH_LOCATION_0_591_37786
--     FISH_LOCATION_1_329_25786
--     FISH_LOCATION_1_422_22179
--   17 AV_* named points (Alterac Valley). Not fishing data. The AV battleground
--     tactics read them, so they need their own decision.
--
-- Idempotency: the whole fish set is replaced, not merged. The DELETE removes
--   every row the loader reads (name LIKE FISH_LOCATION% is the loader own
--   filter), including dungeon or sentinel rows an earlier manual import left
--   behind. The shipped rows then go in, so a re-run ends in the same state.
--   A primary-key INSERT IGNORE would merge with such rows instead: it would
--   keep the excluded rows and double any spots stored under other names.
--   AV_* and every other named location are not touched.
--   The core runs each migration file inside one transaction, so this file
--   has no START TRANSACTION. The INSERT is plain, not IGNORE: a conflict fails
--   the migration loudly instead of skipping rows.

DELETE FROM `ai_playerbot_named_location` WHERE `name` LIKE 'FISH_LOCATION%';

